[:option {:value "154674"} "1,000 metres Time Trial, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "154720"} "Individual Pursuit (4,000 metres), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "154738"} "Team Pursuit (4,000 metres), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "154750"} "Points Race, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "154757"} "Sprint, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "154905"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "155036"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "155164"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "259019"} "2008"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/246"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Individual Pursuit (3,000 metres), Women" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "30 – 31 July 1992"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/678"} "Velódromo de Horta, Barcelona"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/154781"} "17 from 17 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "This was the début for this event at the Olympics, although women had competed in World Championships in the pursuit since 1958. The early stars of the event never had a chance to compete at the Olympics, such as Britain’s great female rider Beryl Burton, Belgium’s Yvonne Reynders, and five-time World Champion Tamara Garkuskin of the Soviet Union. Since 1982 the event had been dominated by two women – France’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/13167"} "Jeannie Longo"] " and America’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/13247"} "Rebecca Twigg"] ". Twigg was World Champion in 1982, 1984-85 and 1987, while Longo won the Worlds in 1986 and 1988-89. But the 1990 World title went to Holland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/13253"} "Leontien van Moorsel"] " while the 1991 World Champion was Germany’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/13213"} "Petra Roßner"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Seventeen riders started the qualifying which was won surprisingly by Australia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/13264"} "Kathy Watt"] ", with Twigg second and Roßner third. The best race of the event occurred in the second quarter-final when Twigg and Longo were drawn against each other. Twigg advanced, winning by less than 4/100th’s of a second. But in the semi-finals, Watt won easily over Twigg and Roßner won the other semi to advance to the final. Watt startd the final quickly and built up of a lead of over 2.3 seconds. However, Roßner rode steadily and caught her with 2½ laps to go, eventually winning by almost two seconds."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "QF"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/13213"} "Petra Roßner"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "3:43.091 (1 h9)"] [:td {} "3:41.509 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "3:48.517 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "3:41.753 (1 h1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/13264"} "Kathy Watt"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {} "3:41.886 (1 h6)"] [:td {} "3:45.305 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "3:49.790 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "3:43.438 (2 h1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {